// @test regression/INV177-once-syntax-errors
// @description A `once` block has no value and no else. TV rejects `x = once cond` with a dedicated message anchored at the `once` token, and an `else` after a once block with 'Syntax error at input "new line"' at column 1 of the else line. Both blocks are still consumed so the rest of the file parses. Probed 2026-09-07, see INV177.
// @expects parse: fail
// @expects error: line=4, column=5, message=/A `once` statement cannot return a value or be assigned to a variable/
// @expects error: line=8, column=1, message=/Syntax error at input "new line"/

//@version=6
indicator("INV177 once syntax")
var int n = 0
x = once close > open
    1
once close > open
    n := 3
else
    n := 4
plot(n + x)
